Backport of upstream sudo-rs PR #830 to the 0.2.2 in ubuntu 24.04.

sudo-rs 0.2.2 builds `libc::sigaction` with struct-literal syntax. On s390x
that struct carries a private `__glibc_reserved0` field (glibc's s390x ABI has
a reserved int between the handler union and `sa_flags`), so the literal does
not compile:

    error: cannot construct `sigaction` with struct literal syntax due to private fields
      --> src/system/signal/set.rs:34:18
       = note: ...and other private field `__glibc_reserved0` that was not provided

This is why noble has no s390x binary for sudo-rs: the archive build hit the
same wall (LP #27776116). Upstream fixed it in 0.2.3 by zero-initialising and
assigning members instead; noble is frozen at 0.2.2 so it will never get that.

Refs: https://github.com/trifectatechfoundation/sudo-rs/issues/829
      https://github.com/trifectatechfoundation/sudo-rs/pull/830

The change is arch-independent -- it applies and compiles on every
architecture, so the test applies it unconditionally.

diff --git a/src/system/signal/set.rs b/src/system/signal/set.rs
--- a/src/system/signal/set.rs
+++ b/src/system/signal/set.rs
@@ -30,14 +30,13 @@ impl SignalAction {
             }
         };
 
-        Ok(Self {
-            raw: libc::sigaction {
-                sa_sigaction,
-                sa_mask: sa_mask.raw,
-                sa_flags,
-                sa_restorer: None,
-            },
-        })
+        // SAFETY: sigaction is a C struct, all-zeroes is a valid representation.
+        let mut raw: libc::sigaction = unsafe { std::mem::zeroed() };
+        raw.sa_sigaction = sa_sigaction;
+        raw.sa_mask = sa_mask.raw;
+        raw.sa_flags = sa_flags;
+
+        Ok(Self { raw })
     }
 
     pub(super) fn register(&self, signal: SignalNumber) -> io::Result<Self> {
